This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
## 1. Primary Request and Intent

The user's requests evolved across distinct phases:

**Phase 1 — Build a Flutter prototype.** "make worktree. create a flutter app... i want to test the interactions on flutter app. create a minimal (very very minimal) reprodction of this app." Three interactions:
- Main screen = capture screen, type immediately
- Swipe right **anywhere** (not just left edge) → menu appears; swipe left → back to the *same note and same scroll position*, "so like dont unmount the main screen"
- Swipe up → first scroll to end of current note, then inverted pull-to-refresh: an indicator appears, "я вижу например ярлычок который тянется", pull past a threshold, release → move to a fresh blank note

Rationale: "it *kinda* works in existing react native app but it doesn't capture my geastures well"

**Phase 2 — Advise on the RN app.** "if i asked you how you can instead make it better on my original react native app - what would you do?"

**Phase 3 — Fix the RN app.** "попробуй теперь улучшить мой rn версию" — after reporting swipe-up and swipe-right are recognized "через раз" (every other time).

**Phase 4 — Install RN app on simulator for comparison.** "а можешь ее тоже на айос симулятор установить? сделаю сравнение"

**Phase 5 — Global rework.** After seeing the RN version was not adaptive ("как только ты на 1% двигаешь - все - транзишн проходит"): "как мне добиться такого же в моем рн? я не против более глобального реворка если он поможет". Then "ок приступай к Б" / "делай".

**Explicit process instructions from the user:**
- "сначала закомить текущее (как эксперемент, на отдельной ветке) а потом сделай как надо"
- "но закомиться перед этим" (before starting Part B)
- "возможно добавим логгинг. и я буду тестить. и когда не пройдет - я тебе скажу и ты чекнешь последний swipe attempt и поймешь почему"
- "тока убери щас ошибку в симуляторе. я прошлую версию тоже тестану"

## 2. Key Technical Concepts

**Flutter:** GestureArena, `GestureDisposition`, `HorizontalDragGestureRecognizer`, `TapAndHorizontalDragGestureRecognizer`, `eagerVictoryOnDrag`, `DeviceGestureSettings`/`gestureSettings`, `debugPrintGestureArenaDiagnostics`, `HitTestBehavior.translucent`, Stack topmost-first hit-testing, `BouncingScrollPhysics` + `AlwaysScrollableScrollPhysics`, `ScrollNotification.depth`, `TestGesture.moveBy(timeStamp:)`.

**React Native:** react-native-gesture-handler (`Gesture.Pan`, `Gesture.Race`, `Gesture.Simultaneous`, `manualActivation`, `manager.activate()/fail()`, `activeOffsetX`, `failOffsetX`, `failOffsetY`, `hitSlop`), react-native-screens (`RNSPanGestureRecognizer`, `gestureResponseDistance`, `fullScreenGestureEnabled`, `isInGestureResponseDistance`), Reanimated (`useSharedValue`, `useAnimatedStyle`, `useAnimatedScrollHandler` with `onScroll`/`onEndDrag`, `runOnJS`, `withTiming`, `interpolateColor`, worklets on the UI runtime = iOS main thread), React Navigation native-stack, `BackHandler`.

**Core architectural insight (stated repeatedly):** The Flutter prototype is reliable not because Flutter arbitrates better, but because its design has **nothing to arbitrate** — the menu is a sibling layer (not a navigation transition) and the pull is the scroll view's own overscroll (not a competing recognizer). The RN app had a competitor at every step. "реворк — это не «выиграть лучше», а «убрать соперника»."

## 3. Files and Code Sections

### Flutter prototype (`experiments/gesture_lab/`) — committed `c01cecf3`

**`lib/gestures.dart`** — the custom recognizer that replaces first-past-the-post with an explicit directional verdict:
```dart
class DirectionalHorizontalDragRecognizer extends HorizontalDragGestureRecognizer {
  DirectionalHorizontalDragRecognizer({
    super.debugOwner,
    this.verticalBailout = 8.0,
    this.horizontalCommit = 12.0,
    this.dominanceRatio = 1.2,
  });
  final Map<int, Offset> _travel = <int, Offset>{};

  @override
  void handleEvent(PointerEvent event) {
    if (event is PointerMoveEvent) {
      final Offset total = (_travel[event.pointer] ?? Offset.zero) + event.delta;
      _travel[event.pointer] = total;
      gestureDebug.axis.value = '${total.dx.toStringAsFixed(0)},${total.dy.toStringAsFixed(0)}';
      if (total.dy.abs() > verticalBailout &&
          total.dy.abs() > total.dx.abs() * dominanceRatio) {
        _travel.remove(event.pointer);
        resolve(GestureDisposition.rejected);   // concede to the scrollable
        return;
      }
      if (total.dx.abs() > horizontalCommit &&
          total.dx.abs() > total.dy.abs() * dominanceRatio) {
        resolve(GestureDisposition.accepted);   // acceptGesture replays pending offset
      }
    }
    super.handleEvent(event);
  }
}
```
Also holds `GestureDebug` (ValueNotifiers for the HUD: `visible`, `axis`, `menu`, `pull`, `armed`, `phase`).

**`lib/capture_page.dart`** — `NoteModel` (index + `TextEditingController` + `FocusNode`, owned by the shell so state survives), `kPullThreshold = 80.0`, `kTabHeight = 44.0`. The pull rides overscroll:
```dart
bool _onScroll(ScrollNotification n) {
  if (n.depth != 0 || n.metrics.axis != Axis.vertical) return false;
  final double over = n.metrics.pixels - n.metrics.maxScrollExtent;
  _pull.value = over > 0 ? over : 0;
  ...
}
void _onRelease(PointerEvent _) {   // raw Listener, not ScrollEndNotification
  if (!widget.live || !_armed) return;
  _armed = false; HapticFeedback.mediumImpact(); widget.onPullCommit();
}
```
TextField uses `scrollPhysics: const NeverScrollableScrollPhysics()` so the outer `SingleChildScrollView` owns every vertical drag; physics is `AlwaysScrollableScrollPhysics(parent: BouncingScrollPhysics())`.

**`lib/main.dart`** — `_ShellState` with `_menu` and `_commit` AnimationControllers. **The critical fix** — the swipe layer is the second-to-last Stack child, not an ancestor:
```dart
Positioned.fill(
  child: RawGestureDetector(
    behavior: HitTestBehavior.translucent,
    gestures: <Type, GestureRecognizerFactory>{
      DirectionalHorizontalDragRecognizer: GestureRecognizerFactoryWithHandlers<...>(...)
    },
  ),
),
const _Hud(),
```

**`test/widget_test.dart`** — 4 tests, all passing. `dragInSteps` threads a real clock because `TestGesture.moveBy` defaults `timeStamp: Duration.zero`.

**`experiments/gesture_lab/README.md`** — documents the arena finding, the rejected alternatives (gestureSettings never plumbed; `enableInteractiveSelection: false` doesn't remove the recognizer; Listener-outside-the-arena still lets the field move the caret), tunables table, known limits.

### RN app (`apps/mobile/`)

**`src/lib/capture-gesture.ts`** — rewritten twice. Final state (after Part B) exports only: `PULL_THRESHOLD = 80`, `PULL_TAB_HEIGHT = 44`, `PULL_TAB_MAX_STRETCH = 96`, `TOP_SLACK = 4`, `SYNC_RIGHTWARD_FAIL = 8`, `ESCAPE_DRAG = 14`, plus:
```ts
export const overscrollPastEnd = (offsetY, contentHeight, viewportHeight): number => {
  "worklet";
  const maxScroll = Math.max(0, contentHeight - viewportHeight);
  return Math.max(0, offsetY - maxScroll);
};
export const shouldCommitPull = (pull: number): boolean => { "worklet"; return pull >= PULL_THRESHOLD; };
export const pullProgress = (pull: number): number => { "worklet"; return Math.min(1, Math.max(0, pull / PULL_THRESHOLD)); };
export const pullTabReveal = (pull: number): number => {
  "worklet";
  return Math.min(Math.max(0, pull), PULL_TAB_HEIGHT + PULL_TAB_MAX_STRETCH);
};
export const visiblePageHeight = (windowHeight, keyboardHeight): number => { "worklet"; return Math.max(1, windowHeight - keyboardHeight); };
```
Deleted: `COMMIT_FRACTION`, `COMMIT_VELOCITY`, `ACTIVATE_PULL`, `BOTTOM_SLACK`, `isAtScrollBottom`, `RIGHTWARD_FAIL`, `RIGHTWARD_FAIL_RATIO`, `LEFTWARD_FAIL`, `VERTICAL_LATCH`, `VERTICAL_LATCH_RATIO`, `isVerticalCommitted`, `horizontalVerdict`, `HorizontalVerdict`, `shouldCommitFiling`, `BACK_SWIPE_GUTTER`, `NATIVE_BACK_RESPONSE_DISTANCE`, `NATIVE_BACK_BAND_FRACTION`, `nativeBackBandBottom`, `isInNativeBackBand`.

**`src/screens/home-shell.tsx`** (new) — context seam:
```ts
export type HomeShell = {
  menuProgress: SharedValue<number>;  // 0 = capture, 1 = menu
  openMenu: () => void;
  openCapture: () => void;
};
export const useHomeShell = (): HomeShell => { ... throws if outside HomeScreen }
```

**`src/screens/home-screen.tsx`** (new) — root screen mounting both layers permanently. `MENU_PARALLAX = 0.3`, `MENU_DIM = 0.08`, `SETTLE = { duration: 220, easing: Easing.out(Easing.cubic) }`. Contains the Android BackHandler:
```ts
useEffect(() => {
  const subscription = BackHandler.addEventListener("hardwareBackPress", () => {
    if (menuProgress.value > 0.5) return false;   // menu showing: let the OS exit
    openMenu();
    return true;
  });
  return () => subscription.remove();
}, [menuProgress, openMenu]);
```
Renders `<MenuScreen/>` (parallax), a dim layer (`pointerEvents="none"`), then `<CaptureScreen/>` translated by `windowW * menuProgress`.

**`src/screens/capture-screen.tsx`** — heavily modified. Key current content:

The hoisted declarations (this ordering is load-bearing):
```ts
const pull = useSharedValue(0);
const runLog = useCallback((line: string) => { console.log(`[gesture] ${line}`); }, []);
// Both of the above must stay ABOVE the scroll handler.
// useAnimatedScrollHandler serializes its worklet at call time and captures
// whatever these names hold at that moment. Declared below it they capture
// undefined, and the first scroll event dies with "Cannot set property
// 'value' of undefined" on the UI runtime.
// ---- Scroll plumbing ----
```

The scroll handler that replaced `swipeToFile`:
```ts
const onScroll = useAnimatedScrollHandler({
  onScroll: (event) => {
    offsetY.value = event.contentOffset.y;
    contentH.value = event.contentSize.height;
    viewportH.value = event.layoutMeasurement.height;
    indicatorOpacity.value = 1;
    indicatorOpacity.value = withDelay(600, withTiming(0, { duration: 350 }));
    if (!transitioning.value) {
      pull.value = overscrollPastEnd(
        event.contentOffset.y, event.contentSize.height, event.layoutMeasurement.height
      );
    }
  },
  onEndDrag: () => {
    if (transitioning.value || !shouldCommitPull(pull.value)) return;
    const pageHeight = visiblePageHeight(windowH.value, keyboard.height.value);
    transitioning.value = true;
    runOnJS(runLog)(`pull:commit at=${Math.round(pull.value)}`);
    pull.value = 0;
    pageY.value = withTiming(-pageHeight, { duration: 260, easing: Easing.out(Easing.cubic) },
      (finished) => { if (finished) { runOnJS(runFinishCommit)(); } else { transitioning.value = false; } });
  },
});
```

`swipeToMenu` (added in Part A, mirror of `swipeToSync`):
```ts
Gesture.Pan()
  .activeOffsetX(16).failOffsetX(-24).failOffsetY([-24, 24])
  .onBegin(() => { runOnJS(runLog)("menu:begin"); })
  .onStart(() => { runOnJS(runLog)("menu:start"); runOnJS(dismissKeyboard)(); })
  .onUpdate((event) => {
    menuProgress.value = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, event.translationX / Math.max(windowW.value, 1)));
  })
  .onEnd((event, success) => {
    if (!success) { runOnJS(runLog)("menu:cancelled"); menuProgress.value = withTiming(0, {duration:180}); return; }
    const shouldOpen = menuProgress.value > MENU_OPEN_PROGRESS || event.velocityX > MENU_OPEN_VELOCITY;
    runOnJS(runLog)(`menu:end p=${menuProgress.value.toFixed(2)} vx=${Math.round(event.velocityX)} open=${shouldOpen}`);
    menuProgress.value = withTiming(shouldOpen ? 1 : 0, { duration: shouldOpen ? 160 : 180, easing: Easing.out(Easing.cubic) });
  })
  .onFinalize((_event, success) => { runOnJS(runLog)(`menu:finalize success=${success}`); })
```
Constants: `MENU_OPEN_PROGRESS = 0.3`, `MENU_OPEN_VELOCITY = 500`.

Gesture composition is now `Gesture.Simultaneous(keyboardEscape, Gesture.Race(swipeToMenu, swipeToSync))`.

Pull tab styles + JSX (styles `pullPill`, `pullLabel`, `pullLabelOverlay`, `pullStem`), using `interpolateColor(pullProgress(pull.value), [0,1], [theme.colors.surface, theme.colors.accent])` and `translateY: PULL_TAB_HEIGHT - reveal - keyboard.height.value`.

`keyboardEscape`'s `horizontalVerdict` call was replaced with an inline check: `if (Math.abs(dx) > 24 && Math.abs(dx) > Math.abs(dy)) { manager.fail(); return; }`.

**`src/screens/menu-screen.tsx`** — `captureProgress`, `menuDepthStyle`, `dimStyle`, `capturePreviewStyle`, `openCaptureBehindPreview`, `runOpenCapture`, `MENU_PARALLAX`, the whole capture-replica JSX and its styles (`dim`, `capturePreview`, `previewPlaceholder`, `previewButton`, `previewMic`) all deleted. `swipeToCapture` now writes `menuProgress.value = 1 - closed`. `pressWasSwipe()` now reads `menuProgress.value < 0.999`. `openCapture` → `closeMenu` calling shell's `openCapture`.

**`src/App.tsx`** — `Menu` + `Capture` screens replaced by one `Home` screen with `headerShown: false`; `BOOT_NAVIGATION_STATE` and `initialState` removed; `initialRouteName="Home"`. Also the demo banner bug fix:
```jsx
{demoMode ? (
  // Purely informational, and it sits across the bottom edge — exactly
  // where a swipe up to file starts. Without this it swallows those
  // touches and the gesture silently never begins.
  <View pointerEvents="none" style={[styles.demoBanner, { backgroundColor: theme.colors.accent }]}>
```

**`src/navigation.ts`** — `RootStackParamList` lost `Menu` and `Capture`, gained `Home: undefined`. `useClearInstantParam` now typed for `"Sync"` only.

**`apps/mobile/GESTURES.md`** — updated three times: Round 2 findings section, "What the screen does now" rewritten twice, alternative A retitled "**adopted**", gestures table now lists two pans with a note that filing is not a gesture.

## 4. Errors and fixes

1. **Flutter: horizontal swipe test failed (capture x = 0).** Wrong hypotheses twice. Fixed by instrumenting (`debugPrintGestureArenaDiagnostics`) which showed `TapAndHorizontalDragGestureRecognizer` "Self-declared winner". Real fix: swipe layer as a translucent `Positioned.fill` Stack sibling above the pages instead of an ancestor.

2. **Flutter bisect harness returned `[]` for every case** — the harness child sized to zero under loose Scaffold constraints. Fixed with `SizedBox.expand` + `Stack(fit: StackFit.expand)`.

3. **Flutter: `MediaQuery` + `DeviceGestureSettings(touchSlop: 44)` was inert** — confirmed from Flutter source that `TextSelectionGestureDetector` never assigns `gestureSettings`. Reverted.

4. **Flutter tests: velocity always zero** — `TestGesture.moveBy` defaults `timeStamp: Duration.zero`. Fixed `dragInSteps` to pass an incrementing clock.

5. **Flutter test: close-swipe started off-screen** — used `find.byType(MenuPage)` as the start point instead.

6. **Ran prettier with no repo config → 162 lines of churn in `settings-screen.tsx`.** Detected via `git diff --stat`. Verified the repo isn't prettier-formatted (neither default nor `--trailing-comma es5` matched untouched files). Reverted all 7 source files with `git checkout --` and re-applied only semantic edits via python. **Lesson: don't run formatters the project doesn't use.**

7. **Python edit script anchor spanned two non-adjacent blocks** (`NATIVE_BACK_BAND_FRACTION` block + `isVerticalCommitted`) → `MISS`. Split into separate replacements. The `edit()` helper is atomic (writes only after all pairs match), so nothing was half-applied.

8. **Regex deleting dead styles mangled `StyleSheet.create`** in menu-screen — `\n  key: \{\n(?:.*\n)*?  \},` ate across entries. Repaired the specific damaged region by hand.

9. **`Animated.View` still used after removing the `Animated` default import** — converted the two static wrappers to plain `View`.

10. **RN runtime: `Cannot set property 'value' of undefined`** at `pull.value = overscrollPastEnd(...)`. Cause: `pull` and `runLog` declared *below* `useAnimatedScrollHandler`, which serializes its worklet at call time. Fixed by hoisting both above the handler with a warning comment.

11. **Metro: `Unable to resolve "expo"`** → worktree had no `node_modules` (npx was fetching on the fly). Ran `npm install` at worktree root.

12. **Metro wouldn't start: port 8081 busy** → my own stale `expo run:ios` process. Verified ownership via `ps` before killing.

13. **External SSD unmounted twice.** First time: disk present but encrypted+locked; handed the user `! diskutil apfs unlockVolume disk5s1` to run themselves — "Пароль я у тебя не спрашиваю и в сессию не тяну." Second time: Metro died (exit 7), commits verified intact.

**User feedback that changed my approach:**
- "бля. я не понимаю. что от меня то требуется?" — I was dumping analysis and offloading diagnosis onto them. I switched to "Ничего. Делаю сам."
- "я не против более глобального реворка если он поможет" — authorized the architectural rework over threshold tuning.
- "сначала закомить текущее (как эксперемент, на отдельной ветке)" and "но закомиться перед этим" — commit checkpoints before invasive work.
- The user rejected my `git fsck` investigation twice and chose "1" (just restart Metro).

## 5. Problem Solving

**Solved:** Flutter arena conflict (hit-test ordering); Flutter test harness velocity trap; RN asymmetric `horizontalVerdict` killing arcing swipe-ups; RN back-swipe being two implementations split by height; the demo banner swallowing swipe-up touches; the `node_modules` / Metro setup; the non-adaptive back swipe (Part A); the `manualActivation` blocker causing 2-in-10 horizontal swipe loss (Part B, diagnosed from the real Metro log).

**Diagnosed from the live `[gesture]` log** — the decisive evidence:
```
menu:begin
file:down x=241 y=299
file:release->menu dx=37 dy=1
menu:finalize success=false     ← no menu:start
```
vs a success at `dx=33`. Conclusion: not a threshold, a race — `manager.fail()` is terminal for the whole touch, so whether `swipeToMenu` survives depends on whether one more pointer move arrives. Also the 8pt window between `activeOffsetX(16)` and release at `dx > 24` where `swipeToMenu` is eligible but blocked.

**Open/unresolved:**
- `git fsck` reported `empty filename in tree entry` / `badTree`. Not investigated (user declined). I advised that a `git clone` or push to a remote is a better integrity check than fsck.
- Android has no ScrollView bounce, so **the pull gesture does not exist on Android** after Part B. Flagged explicitly as an unpaid cost.
- `gesture-trace.ts` + its Settings → Diagnostics readout are orphaned (no producer) after Part B. Flagged; offered to delete or keep.
- `package-lock.json` (2 lines), `ios/Podfile.lock`, `ios/Type.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj` are dirty and deliberately uncommitted.

## 6. All user messages

1. "make worktree. create a flutter app. look, i want to test the interactions on flutter app. create a minimal (very very minimal) reprodction of this app. what i want to do is / main screen. i swipe right (like almost anywhere on the screen, not just from the left edge) - the menu appears. i swipe back to the left - i land back on the capture screen (ideally on the same note and same scroll position so like dont unmount the main screen) / main screen is the capture screen / and i can write notes. and i can swipe up - and i start a new note (like first - i should be able to scroll to the end of the current note. and then it's like a "pull-to-refresh" mechanics - i see some indicator that i'm "starting an action to move to the next note", then i kinda "pull" (here from the bottom to up not from the up to bottom as in usual pull-to-refresh mechanics) - я вижу например ярлычок который тянется - then i need to "pull" up to a certain treshold (like certain distance from when the action "started"). and when i done it - i can release so it moves to the next note (fresh screen where i can start a new note) / it *kinda* works in existing react native app but it doesn't capture my geastures well / so yep. very minimal just to test those actions interaction"
